Is 'worker' guaranteed to print before this complete program exits? Identify the bug and fix it.

```go
package main
import ("fmt"; "sync")
func main() {
    var wg sync.WaitGroup
    go func() {
        wg.Add(1)
        defer wg.Done()
        fmt.Println("worker")
    }()
    wg.Wait()
}
```

Does this complete program terminate normally? Explain and suggest a structural fix.

```go
package main
import "fmt"
func main() {
    jobs := make(chan int)
    results := make(chan int)
    go func() {
        for j := range jobs { results <- j * 2 }
        close(results)
    }()
    jobs <- 1
    jobs <- 2
    close(jobs)
    for r := range results { fmt.Println(r) }
}
```

